cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Minimum Sufficient Compute (MSC)"
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bonal
    given-names: Shanmukesh
repository-code: "https://github.com/NewUser4622/minimum-sufficient-compute"
abstract: >-
  Per-sample, cost-normalised measurement of the compute a trained network
  needs, and an analysis of oracle upper bounds for early-exit inference.
  Oracle bounds are shown to exceed the accuracy of the network they bound
  (+6.86 pt on CIFAR-100 over 90 runs; +7.39 and +6.91 pt on ImageNet-100 at
  224 px including a vision transformer), with the excess growing as the exits
  improve.
keywords:
  - early exit
  - adaptive inference
  - example difficulty
  - oracle bounds
license: MIT
